<%# One setting of the run, read back in the field the form asks for it in: its label, the
    tooltip saying what it meant, and the one answer this run gave, in a select holding
    that answer alone. The details page asks for this four times over; written out at each
    of them it was the same twenty lines four times.

    locals:
      id:      ties the label to its select, and is what a spec looks the field up by
      label:   the setting's name, spelled the way the form spells it
      value:   this run's answer
      tooltip: what the setting meant for the run, or nil where the form offers no help.
               Squished here so a caller can wrap a long one across source lines without
               the indentation reaching the tooltip. %>
<%= label_tag id, class: 'form-label' do %>
  <%= label %>

  <% if tooltip.present? %>
    <span data-bs-toggle='tooltip' data-bs-title='<%= tooltip.squish %>'>
      <i class='bi bi-question-circle' aria-label='helper text'></i>
    </span>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%= select_tag nil, options_for_select([value]), class: 'form-select mb-3', id:, name: nil %>
